<title>What's New in CSPro 8.1?</title>
<context ID_HELP_WHAT_IS_NEW />

This is a detailed list of changes in CSPro 8.1. For a more general overview, see the <i>readme.txt</i> file located in the CSPro installation folder.


<subheader>General</subheader>

<list>
    <li>CSPro is now open source! The source code, written in C++, JavaScript, Java/Kotlin, and PHP, with some code written in C#, is available on GitHub: <link https://<definition csprousers_github />><definition csprousers_github /></link>.</li>
    <li>A new dialog, <link manage_application_files.csdoc>Manage Application Files</link>, replaces the Add Files and Drop Files dialogs, providing a central place to manage an application's files and each file's properties. New properties include:~!~~!~
        <list>
            <li><link properties_application.csdoc>Application</link>: the name and label can be modified.</li>
            <li><link change_dictionary_properties.csdoc>Dictionary</link>: options to allow external dictionaries to be synchronized as part of a <link synchronization_simple.csdoc>Simple Synchronization routine</link> and to build <link value_set_images.csdoc>value set images</link> into a <link binary_data_entry_application_file_pen.csdoc>compiled application (.pen)</link>.</li>
            <li><link change_message_properties.csdoc>Messages</link>: the message type&mdash;user-defined or system overrides&mdash;is now specified as a property, no longer based on the filename starting with "CSProRuntime".</li>
            <li><link change_report_properties.csdoc>Report</link>: <link templated_reports.csdoc>~~ fills</link> can be escaped for writing to CSV format.</li>
            <li><link resources.csdoc>Resources</link>: in addition to directories, it is now possible to add single files as resources, and options provide control over what files in directories are processed.</li>
        </list></li>
    <li>The CSPro Settings dialog has been renamed <link manage_credentials.csdoc>Manage Credentials</link> and now allows for the granular clearing of synchronization, data, and location credentials.</li>
    <li>Numeric value sets can be generated in <link generate_numeric_value_set.csdoc>descending order</link>.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Android</subheader>

<list>
    <li>CSEntry can be <link android_launching_csentry_from_other_applications.csdoc>launched using a deep link</link> that starts with <colorinline Kotlin>"https://csprousers.org/pff"</colorinline>. CSEntry runs the application specified as part of the deep link's path.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Mapping</subheader>

<list>
    <li>Offline maps can now use ArcGIS Tile Packages that use the <link "https://enterprise.arcgis.com/en/server/10.8/publish-services/linux/inside-the-compact-cache-storage-format.htm">CompactV2 storage format</link> (with the file extension .tpkx).</li>
    <li>On Windows, ArcGIS Tile Packages created using the <link "https://desktop.arcgis.com/en/arcmap/10.3/map/working-with-arcmap/about-tile-packages.htm">Mixed tile format</link> ("JPEG in the center of the package with PNG 32 on the edge of the package") are supported.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Logic</subheader>

<list>
    <li>The <logiccolor>Image</logiccolor> object can now load <link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICO_(file_format)">icon files (.ico)</link> on Windows and can <link Image_save_function.csdoc>save</link> to that format on all platforms.</li>
    <li>If an <logiccolor>Array</logiccolor> object is defined with initial values and is also marked as a <link Array_statement.csdoc>saved array</link>, the initial values will only be used if the array does not exist in the <link saved_arrays_file_sva.csdoc>saved array file</link>.</li>
    <li>The <logiccolor>Symbol.updateValueFromJson</logiccolor> function has been renamed <logiccolor>Symbol.setValueFromJson</logiccolor>, though the old name will remain as an alias for some time.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Action Invoker</subheader>

<list>
    <li>A new action, <action>throwException</action>, throws an exception in the current execution environment.</li>
    <li>A new action, <action>System.createShortcut</action>, creates a shortcut to a CSPro application or file. The shortcut is placed on the Windows Desktop, or on the Android launcher.</li>
    <li>The <action>UI.closeDialog</action> action has been renamed <action>UI.close</action>, though the old name will remain as an alias for some time. A new argument allows the <link html_dialog_ui.csdoc>HTML dialog</link> or <link html_in_cspro.csdoc>web view</link> to be closed without a valid result but instead with an exception that is thrown in the execution environment that launched the dialog or web view.</li>
    <li>The <link action_invoker_execution_json.csdoc>JSON format of exceptions</link> has changed from a string to an object with <link CS_throwException.csdoc>message, name, and cause</link> properties.</li>
    <li>Binary data can be <link action_invoker_binary_data.csdoc>cached</link>, an optimization useful when binary data will be used by multiple actions.</li>
    <li><link action_invoker_resource_ids.csdoc>Resource IDs</link>, such as those used by the <action>Sqlite</action> namespace's actions, do not need to be specified when they can be <link action_invoker_resource_ids.csdoc>calculated implicitly</link>.</li>
    <li>The <action>Sqlite</action> namespace's database resource ID argument is now named <arg>dbId</arg>. The old name, <arg>db</arg>, will work in CSPro 8.1 but not in future versions.</li>
    <li>The <action>Logic.updateSymbolValue</action> action has been renamed <action>Logic.setSymbolValue</action>, though the old name will remain as an alias for some time.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Tools</subheader>

<list>
    <li>The <link ParadataConcat::introduction_to_paradata_concatenator.csdoc>Paradata Concatenator</link> and <logiccolor>paradata</logiccolor> function's concatenation routines have been optimized, improving performance when processing many paradata logs.</li>
</list>


<seealso what_is_new_in_cspro.csdoc />
